# Local assistant instructions. The same content is tracked as AGENTS.md, which
# is the vendor-neutral convention; this file is kept on disk for tooling that
# looks for it by name and is deliberately not part of the repository.
CLAUDE.md
frontend/CLAUDE.md

# the scrub script is a one-time local tool, not part of the project
scrub-history.sh

# Official Agora quickstart.
#
# No longer "reference only": the SDK path in backend/app/voice_agent.py is
# adapted from server/src/agent.py, the vendor chain (Deepgram nova-3 +
# gpt-4o-mini + MiniMax, all Agora-managed) is copied from it, and
# web/src/lib/conversation.ts is what identified the uid-"0" sentinel that was
# dropping every human transcript. Committing the source keeps that provenance
# checkable.
#
# The SOURCE is small — server/ is 14 files, web/ is 55. What is not committed
# is the installed dependency tree: my-python-demo alone is 1,084 MB across
# 33,620 files, which GitHub would reject and every future clone would pay for.
agent-quickstart-python/my-python-demo/
agent-quickstart-python/**/venv/
agent-quickstart-python/**/.venv/
agent-quickstart-python/**/node_modules/

# Root env file. This held a LIVE AGORA_APP_CERTIFICATE and reached GitHub
# in commit e122b5f - see docs/session_log.md. The certificate mints tokens
# for the whole Agora project, so it is rotated, not merely deleted.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Local SQLite databases and WAL journal files
backend/data/*.db
backend/data/*.db-wal
backend/data/*.db-shm
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
